    <DataNode elementId="AT5G52560-MONOMER" textLabel="UDP-sugar pyrophosphorylase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9C5I1" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="1050" centerY="635" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">|FRAME: AT5G52560-MONOMER USP| is a UDP-sugar pyrophosphorylase with a broad substrate specificity |CITS: [16757173][17341835]|. Therefore it is likely to participate in several related nucleotide sugar salvage pathways. It may also contribute to the &lt;i&gt;de novo&lt;/i&gt; biosynthesis of |FRAME: UDP-GLUCURONATE UDP-GlcA| via the |FRAME: PWY-4841| pathway |CITS: [16757173]|. In one study, it was shown to have a preference for |FRAME: CPD-510| in the forward direction and |FRAME: UDP-GLUCURONATE| in the reverse direction &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt;. The enzyme also had a strict preference for |FRAME: UTP| as a nucleotide donor and required |FRAME: MN+2| or |FRAME: MG+2| but did not function with |FRAME: CA+2| |CITS: [16757173]|. There is some disagreement about whether the enzyme acts on |FRAME: CPD-1825| and |FRAME: CPD-490| at physiologically relevant levels |CITS: [16757173][17341835]|. There was also no direct characterization of the ability of USP to act on |FRAME: CPD-501| (GalA-1-P), however, if purified recombinant USP is added to a reaction mixture containing the products of |FRAME: AT3G10700-MONOMER GalAK|, including |FRAME: CPD-501 GalA-1-P|, then |FRAME: UDP-D-GALACTURONATE| is formed |CITS: [19509290]|. Expression analysis indicates that |FRAME: AT5G52560-MONOMER USP| transcripts are present in Arabidopsis seedlings, rosettes, and inflorescences and |FRAME: 2.7.7.44-RXN UDP-glucuronate pyrophosphorylase| activity can also be detected in these organs and tissues although it cannot be conclusively attributed to |FRAME: AT5G52560-MONOMER USP| |CITS: [16757173]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G52560-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT5G52560.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Panther" value="PTHR11952" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pride" value="Q9C5I1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Smr" value="Q9C5I1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pfam" value="PF01704" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Interpro" value="IPR029044" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q9C5I1" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33981, RXN-T9-1907, RXN-T9-1906, RXN-10544, RXN-10543, RXN-10542, RXN-12850" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="7" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT5G52560.1" />
      <Property key="FunctionalAssignmentStatus" value=":PROBABLE-ENZYME" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT5G52560" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightExp" value="69." />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightKd" value="69." />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_16757173" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_19509290" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT2G19860-MONOMER" textLabel="Hexokinase-2" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="P93834" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="1200" centerY="635" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; gene &lt;i&gt;HXK2&lt;/i&gt; was selected for its ability to complement the phenotype of the &lt;i&gt;hxk1 hxk2&lt;/i&gt; yeast double mutant, which completely lacks hexokinase (HXK) activity. The gene allowed the recombinant yeast strains to grown on media supplemented with fructose |CITS:[9014361]|. In spite of their ability to confer fructose utilization to the recombinant yeast, the enzyme encoded by this gene is unlikely to be a fructokinase as it is able to phosphorylate glucose (data not shown in |CITS:[9014361]|). A later study showed that its paralog |FRAME:AT4G29130-MONOMER| was indeed able to catalyze the phosphorylation of both glucose and fructose |CITS:[10402427]|, although the enzyme shows a definite preference for the former. This, however, has not been demonstrated for the enzyme encoded by &lt;i&gt;HXK2&lt;/i&gt;.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT2G19860-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT2G19860.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="P93834" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Panther" value="PTHR19443" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Smr" value="P93834" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Prints" value="PR00475" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pride" value="P93834" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Interpro" value="IPR022672" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pfam" value="PF03727" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Phylomedb" value="P93834" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Prosite" value="PS51748" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pid" value="AAB49911" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Swissmodel" value="P93834" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-ARA-544, RXN-13709, RXN-7280, RXN-4904" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="4" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT2G19860.1" />
