      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="715" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">SSIV (SS4) is a soluble starch synthase that is required for normal |FRAME: CPD-7043| formation |CITS: [19666739][17217470]|. SSIV appears to play a role in starch granule initiation |CITS: [23393426]|.</Comment>
