    <DataNode elementId="AT1G35580-MONOMER" textLabel="Alkaline/neutral invertase CINV1" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT1G35580-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="600" centerY="795" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">CINV1 functions as an alkaline/neutral invertase in &lt;i&gt;in vitro assays&lt;/i&gt; and plants with a mutation in the CINV1 gene have reduced invertase activity |CITS: [17220200][21441406]|. The question of whether this enzyme should be categorized as neutral or alkaline has not yet been conclusively determined because different pH optima were reported in two different papers. One falls in the neutral range (pH 7.0-8.0) |CITS: [17220200]| while the other falls into the alkaline range (pH ~9.5) |CITS: [21441406]|. However, the K&lt;sub&gt;m&lt;/sub&gt; values for sucrose reported in the two papers are quite similar: (~9.9 mM) |CITS: [17220200]| and (8.4 mM) |CITS: [21441406]|. The enzyme appears to be primarily cytosolic, but can also be detected in the nucleus and at membranes when expressed as an RFP fusion protein |CITS: [17220200]|. CINV1, |FRAME: AT4G09510-MONOMER CINV2|, and possibly other cytosolic invertases may play an important role in supplying carbon from sucrose to non-photosynthetic tissues |CITS: [19470642]|. &lt;i&gt;atinvg&lt;/i&gt; mutants have reduced root growth, reduced invertase activity, and increased expression of antioxidant genes under basal conditions. The levels of CINV1 / A/N-InvG transcripts rise in response to a hydrogen peroxide treatment |CITS: [21441406]|. These findings suggest that A/N-InvG may play a role in maintaining reactive oxygen species homeostasis in Arabidopsis cells |CITS: [21441406]|. CINV1 / A/N-INVG has been shown to interact with |FRAME:AT3G09920 PIP5K9|, a phosphatidylinositol monophosphate kinase |CITS: [17220200]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G35580-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="Alkaline/neutral invertase G" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="A/N-INVG" />
      <Property key="Synonym_3" value="Cytosolic invertase 1" />
      <Property key="Synonym_4" value="AtCYT-INV1" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33619, RXN-291" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="2" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0005829, GO:0016020, GO:0005634" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT1G35580.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT1G35580" />
      <Property key="^citations" value="17220200, 17220200, 17220200" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="Locations" value="CCI-CYTOSOL-PL, CCI-NUCLEUS-PL, CCO-MEMBRANE" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_17220200" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_21441406" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_19470642" />
    </DataNode>
