    <DataNode elementId="AT5G22510-MONOMER" textLabel="Alkaline/neutral invertase E, chloroplastic" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT5G22510-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="875" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">A/N-INV-E is an alkaline/neutral invertase based on &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; assays using recombinant protein |CITS: [20304912]| and experiments performed with &lt;i&gt;inve&lt;/i&gt; (SALK_138953) mutants |CITS: [18034262]|. Recombinant A/N-InvE cannot hydrolyze other disaccharides (maltose, lactose, trehalose, cellobiose, and galactinol) &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; |CITS: [20304912]|. Fluorescently-tagged A/N-InvE localizes to the chloroplast |CITS: [18034262]|. Therefore, a truncated version of the protein lacking the putative signal peptide was used for the &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; assays |CITS: [20304912]|. A/N-InvE is implicated in the development of the photosynthetic apparatus and nitrogen assimilation in seedlings |CITS: [20304912]|. &lt;i&gt;inve&lt;/i&gt; mutants also have reduced starch contents suggesting that this enzyme might be involved in carbohydrate storage and/or remobilization processes and may play a role in inter-organeller carbon flows |CITS: [18034262]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G22510-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="A/N-INVE" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33944, RXN-42" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="2" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0009507" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT5G22510.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT5G22510" />
      <Property key="^citations" value="18034262" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="Locations" value="CCI-CHLOROPLAST-PL" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_20304912" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_18034262" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT1G69200.1" textLabel="AT1G69200.1" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT1G69200.1" dataSource="plantcyc" />
