    <DataNode elementId="AT3G01180-MONOMER" textLabel="soluble starch synthase II" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT3G01180-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="1035" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">SSII (SS2) is a soluble starch synthase that is required for normal |FRAME: CPD-7043| formation in conjunction with |FRAME: AT1G11720 SSIII| |CITS: [18811962][21624979]|. SSII appears to have a preference for glucan chains with 13-22 glucosyl units |CITS: [23393426]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT3G01180-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-13724" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0009570, GO:0009507" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT3G01180.1" />
      <Property key="FunctionalAssignmentStatus" value=":PROBABLE-ENZYME" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT3G01180" />
      <Property key="^citations" value="23393426:EV-IC:3572315639:dreher, 18431481:EV-EXP-IDA:3572315587:dreher" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="Locations" value="CCI-CHLOR-STR-PL, CCI-CHLOROPLAST-PL" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_23393426" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT2G35020-MONOMER" textLabel="UDP-N-acetylglucosamine diphosphorylase 2" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="O64765" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="1035" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">UDP-N-acetylglucosamine (UDP-GlcNAc) is an essential precursor for glycoprotein and glycolipid biosynthesis in plants and it can also serve as a regulatory modification on signaling proteins. This enzyme, GlcNAc1pUT2, is capable of synthesizing |FRAME: UDP-N-ACETYL-D-GLUCOSAMINE| (UDP-GlcNAc) from |FRAME: UTP| and |FRAME: N-ACETYL-D-GLUCOSAMINE-1-P| &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; |CITS: [20557289]|. It can also catalyze the reverse reaction using |FRAME: UDP-N-ACETYL-D-GLUCOSAMINE UDP-GlcNAc| and the less common 4-epimer, |FRAME: UDP-N-ACETYL-GALACTOSAMINE| (UDP-GalNAc) |CITS: [20557289]|. In addition, unlike the related protein |FRAME: AT1G31070-MONOMER GlcNAc1pUT1|, this enzyme can also act on |FRAME: GLC-1-P|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT2G35020-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT2G35020.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Panther" value="PTHR11952" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pride" value="O64765" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Smr" value="O64765" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pfam" value="PF01704" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Interpro" value="IPR029044" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="O64765" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="N-acetylglucosamine-1-phosphate uridylyltransferase 2" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="UDP-N-acetylgalactosamine diphosphorylase 2" />
      <Property key="Synonym_3" value="UTP--glucose-1-phosphate uridylyltransferase 2" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33739, RXN-33738, RXN-T9-2226, RXN-12846, RXN-12845" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="5" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT2G35020.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT2G35020" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_20557289" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT5G24300-MONOMER" textLabel="Starch synthase 1, chloroplastic/amyloplastic" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9FNF2" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="1035" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">SSI (SS1) is a soluble starch synthase involved in the formation of |FRAME: CPD-7043 amylopectin|. It preferentially acts on glucan chains that have 9-10 glucans |CITS: [23393426]|. Analyses of the phenotype of &lt;i&gt;ss1&lt;/i&gt; mutants suggest that this enzyme plays an important role in transient starch biosynthesis in the leaves |CITS: [16045475 ]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G24300-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT5G24300.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Cazy" value="GT5" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pride" value="Q9FNF2" />
