    <DataNode elementId="AT2G36190-MONOMER" textLabel="cell wall invertase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT2G36190-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="1050" centerY="1115" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">cwINV4 appears to function as a cell wall invertase based on the phenotype of &lt;i&gt;cwinv4&lt;/i&gt; mutants |CITS: [19861655]|. In addition, visualization of a cwINV4:GFP fusion protein provided some evidence of a cell wall localization for the protein |CITS: [19861655]|. cwINV4 transcripts are expressed at high levels in lateral and median nectaries and this enzyme plays an important role in nectar production |CITS: [19861655]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT2G36190-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33741, RXN-12839" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="2" />
