      <Comment source="PMN, zhang">Maltooligosaccharides are glucooligosaccharides derived from D-glucose monomers linked via &amp;alpha;-1,4 bonds as in |FRAME: MALTOSE|. More specifically, the term is applied to linear oligosaccharides composed of more than two and less than ten units of glucose. The corresponding &amp;alpha;-1,6 glucooligosaccharides are called |FRAME: Isomaltooligosaccharides isomaltooligosaccharides|.</Comment>
